From: Rob Lymm <rob@mediaeden.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: keep the shrinker off carveout backed objects

On hardware with no IOMMU, msm hands out pages from a VRAM carveout and
those objects are created with drm_gem_private_object_init(), so they have
no shmem file. Nothing stops the shrinker from taking them.

Purging one reaches the end of msm_gem_purge(), which calls
shmem_truncate_range(file_inode(obj->filp), ...) on a NULL file. On an
Adreno 330 with a 512 MB carveout this kills kswapd inside the GEM locks,
and the compositor then blocks in msm_gem_madvise() forever, which freezes
the display with no way back but a reboot:

    Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000014
    PC is at msm_gem_purge+0x100/0x15c
    Comm: kswapd0
    msm_gem_purge <- purge <- drm_gem_lru_scan <- msm_gem_shrinker_scan
                  <- do_shrink_slab <- shrink_slab <- shrink_node
                  <- balance_pgdat <- kswapd

Evicting one is quieter and worse: put_pages() returns the carveout
allocation, and there is no shmem file to page the contents back in from,
so the object comes back holding whatever the allocator hands out next.

Neither helps the system in any case: carveout pages are reserved at boot
and returning them frees no system memory.

Report both kinds as unpurgeable, which also covers eviction through
is_unevictable().

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.h	2026-09-20 12:24:55.505473724 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.h	2026-09-20 12:24:55.552660742 +0100
@@ -230,6 +230,16 @@
 /* imported/exported objects are not purgeable: */
 static inline bool is_unpurgeable(struct msm_gem_object *msm_obj)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Without an IOMMU the driver hands out pages from the VRAM
+	 * carveout, and those objects have no shmem file behind them.
+	 * The shrinker must leave them alone. Purging one dereferences
+	 * obj->filp, which is NULL, and evicting one frees the only copy
+	 * of its contents: there is nothing to page them back in from.
+	 */
+	if (!msm_obj->base.filp)
+		return true;
+
 	return drm_gem_is_imported(&msm_obj->base) || msm_obj->pin_count;
 }
 
